WEBVTT

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:16.870
Sis! Sis!

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.920
It was you.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.670
Alice.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.300
Karen?!

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.180
So I've failed once again.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.320
Kasane, look out!

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.370
I'll hit reset as many times as it takes.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.630
Wait!

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.800
Did it work?

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.760
No data's been broadcast to us.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.260
They block data from
being transferred here.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.310
Oh, right.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.140
If all of New Himuka has seen this,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:25.270
the streets must be in chaos now.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:34.910
Don't move.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:15.710
Arahabaki's Trap

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.510
Kasane!

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.390
Take it easy.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:23.350
Brain Eater exacts
a heavy toll on your mind.

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:27.100
What the hell is Karen up to?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.810
Did he use the power of time travel?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.320
No, that was teleportation.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.070
He copied her power but didn't use it?

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.610
What if...

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.370
To use the power of time travel...

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.830
Yuito.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:46.830
Karen may need both Kasane
and Yuito's psionic powers.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.420
We have to stop him.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:05.020
Sis, I know you, too,
are worried about Yuito.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:08.890
I'm sorry I couldn't save you.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.320
Thank you for protecting me to the end.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:19.910
Yuito!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.210
Not so fast!

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.710
Pesky little gnats.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.550
Karen.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.510
Karen, you're trying to copy
Yuito's power?! Why now?!

00:04:42.510 --> 00:04:46.010
You lost the element of surprise.
The odds are against you.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.140
Surely, you know.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:53.770
I could reduce you all to a
smoldering pile of ash if I so wished.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.940
If you're after Yuito's power,

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:59.070
you can't use attacks
that would harm his brain.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:02.910
How about I crush your arms
and legs one at a time?

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.370
Or if you'd like to keep your body intact,
let me take your power.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.410
Why do you want it so bad?

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.830
That is on a need-to-know...

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.880
...basis!

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:16.960
We are carrying out
Yakumo Sumeragi's will.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:20.090
We must exact vengeance upon the moon.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.170
The moon?

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.390
What's he talking about?

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:28.010
Even with civilian brains,
brain function can be vastly expanded

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.730
by connecting tens of thousands together.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:35.690
And once we connect such a vast
number of brains to a psionics user,

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:39.230
New Himuka's military might
can be increased exponentially.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.230
"The moon?!"
"What the hell?"

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:43.480
"What's going on?"
"Is this for real?"

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:43.490
You're insane! Only psionics users
can withstand a SAS connection!

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.530
They need not withstand it.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.700
All I care about
is access to their brains.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.370
Secure Arahabaki, now!

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.620
We're being flooded with inquiries.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.500
Chief, the council is demanding
your presence now.

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:27.070
He's too powerful.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:34.710
I knew that, but how can anyone
wield such massive psionic power?

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:37.210
You're tougher than I thought.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:40.340
It's true you have immense
power at your hands.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:43.130
But there's only one of you!

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:45.590
This won't go the way you wanted!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.720
How about you just leave?

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.350
We don't want to fight anymore.

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:53.810
It seems you're mistaken.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:56.730
Only the victorious get to say that.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.080
Wh-What is this?!

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:13.790
I can't move.

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:16.670
You cannot defeat me.

00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:18.670
And especially not here.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.800
These cables are from Arahabaki?!

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.760
It seems I've hacked in.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.260
Karen, what are you doing?!

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:33.140
What is this?

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:41.650
Now I remember. It's like the time
my power resonated with Kasane's.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:41.730
"Danger!"

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:45.150
Yuito, what's wrong?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:54.490
Has Karen gotten deep into his brain?

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.290
It's no use. I can't stop him.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.460
Yuito's psionic power is...

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:19.270
What's that? An earthquake?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.690
Yuito.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:30.360
Arahabaki has taken control of me.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.580
Don't tell me Karen plans to...

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:41.120
From the beginning once again... Alice.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:46.920
He's gone.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:55.810
Yuito!

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:58.560
Yuito!

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.310
Yuito!

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.190
Yuito!

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.270
Yuito!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.110
Snap out of it! Hey!

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.400
Yuito! Yuito!

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:24.960
Alice, it seems you protected
Kasane from Togetsu.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:30.420
You've more than caught up with us.

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:36.510
Now I, too, must do what needs to be done.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:43.650
Major General Fubuki, Togetsu
has deployed more troops.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:45.020
Understood.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:00.250
Am I...?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.920
Yuito! Yuito, hang in there!

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.290
Yuito!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.840
Are we too late?

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.420
Damn it!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:54.510
Karen attacked us.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.380
Only Yuito ended up like this.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:59.720
Karen forced Arahabaki
to invade our minds.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:02.640
That's when something
happened to Yuito's brain.

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:06.020
Yuito.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:10.730
He's suffered brain damage.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.690
Where's Major General Karen?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:17.450
He stole Yuito's power and vanished.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:21.700
W-W-Wait.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:23.750
Wait!

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:33.380
Where are you going?

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.510
Don't go.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.940
No, don't go.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:49.060
Please don't go.

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:10.040
I don't want to forget everyone.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.340
Everyone?

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:15.670
Who is everyone?

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.430
I can't connect via brain talk.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:26.640
Maybe...

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.690
Maybe Yuito's memory is fading.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:31.770
That means...

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.860
His past will be erased?!

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:37.940
Worst case, he'll be
erased from existence.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.030
I don't even wanna think about that.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:42.320
Memories are what define a person.

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.870
Once they're all gone,
Yuito will be gone, too.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.120
We can't let that happen!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.540
Isn't there something we can do?!

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:52.460
We have to think of something!

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:55.710
What if we copied our memories to Yuito?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.550
What do you mean, "copy"?

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:59.420
It could work.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.220
We reload his connection
to us with our memories.

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:05.060
Reload? Care to explain?

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:09.100
We digitize our memories
and load them into Yuito's mind.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:10.440
We can do it via SAS.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.940
That's insane!

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:16.270
Loading other people's memories?
You sure about this?

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:17.860
It's risky.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.530
It's our only choice.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:21.780
We have to anchor his existence.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:25.120
Memory transplantation
was deemed theoretically possible

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:27.870
during research on
personality rehabilitation.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:32.370
Okay, tell me all you know about it.
I'll code the program we'll need.

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:35.840
Whoa, whoa, we're doing this now?!

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.870
Whoa...

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.040
Did you forget who I am?

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:19.380
"Yuito Sumeragi"

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.500
There might still be problems with--

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.420
Then we overcome them!

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.630
I'm willing to do anything to save Yuito!

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:27.850
The pressure's on, eh? Well, bring it.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.970
I don't mind a tough challenge.

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.640
Hanabi, keep talking to Yuito.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:37.110
External stimuli should somewhat
slow his memory loss.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.060
Okay!

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:42.030
Yuito? Yuito! Can you hear me?!

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.490
Okay, the program's done!

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:45.660
Already?!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.160
Let me see.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:50.740
Okay, lemme know how it looks.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.500
This won't cover everything.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.870
We have to stream encoded data,

00:14:54.870 --> 00:15:00.170
and then revalidate, reconfigure,
and embed it as memories.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.720
Right, I totally missed that. Nice catch.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:07.470
The main issue is Yuito's brain structure.

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:10.680
We have to select the right memory areas.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.480
In that case, this should help.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.850
I have Yuito's brain scan data.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.060
Never thought it would prove useful.

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:21.400
Why would you have that?

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:26.280
Remember how you guys kept using
those data terminals in Togetsu?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:29.780
Well, they were stealing
your data the whole time.

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:34.910
But relax. I deleted it all after I
noticed what they were up to.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:39.170
But I did keep a backup just in case.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:40.290
You saved the day.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:44.090
We should be able to set
the right memory areas with this.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.010
"Yuito Sumeragi"

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:54.600
The specified coordinates match
the brain areas with abnormal readings.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:59.850
Then we're right on target.
All that's left is to run the program.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:08.450
Who are you?

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.160
It's me?

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:22.880
Who... Who am I?

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:24.460
Who?

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:37.140
I am... I'm...

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.810
Connect the SAS cables!

00:16:49.530 --> 00:16:52.490
What is this?

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.780
What?!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.590
I put him under.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.430
Well done.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.600
Let's get started.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.480
Remember all you can about Yuito!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.560
Yuito!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.690
Yuito!

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.950
Yuito, Yuito.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:38.910
Yuito, Yuito, Yuito.

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:42.920
Yuito, Yuito, Yuito.

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:46.880
Yuito, Yuito, Yuito.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:05.110
Yuito.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:07.360
Yuito.

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:09.230
Yuito.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.740
Yuito.

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.170
Yuito.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.940
Yuito. There's no time to explain.

00:18:43.940 --> 00:18:46.230
Let me put this on you.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:49.320
You must live.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:54.650
Kasane?

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:01.700
Why... Why am I...?

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:07.630
What is going on?

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:19.010
Dad?

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:26.650
They're calling to me.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:49.000
Now I understand. I have to get back.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.350
Mom?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.430
Yuito.

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:13.440
I'm glad I was finally able to remember.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:22.740
No! Open your eyes, Yuito!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.790
Yuito!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.750
Huh? Was I...?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.800
Was I dreaming?

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:37.130
Hanabi!

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:41.850
Yuito! Are you okay now?

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:44.640
Kasane and... You're all here.

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.350
But why?

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.180
Yuito!

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.610
A curfew has been imposed.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.900
We ask that you ignore
the misinformation being spread.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.860
In accordance with official
government information,

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.780
please stay at home or indoors
until further instructed.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:03.950
Furthermore...

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.740
What misinformation?

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:08.080
"Whaaaaaaat?"
"The moon's gonna attack?!"

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:08.080
Huh? What is he babbling about?

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:14.000
"This is insane!"
"Did the government know about this?"

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:10.000
We can't be outside?!

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:11.420
I heard the moon's gonna attack!

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:13.840
The media's the government's lapdog.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.710
It's treason to defy the government!

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.260
Yeah!

00:21:18.260 --> 00:21:23.720
Once it gets this bad, government
control over information breaks down.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:30.100
Even the most thorough censorship system
can't completely muzzle public opinion.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.690
What about Naomi?

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.270
Oh, right.

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:38.690
My brother is behind all this.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:42.820
Who'd have imagined it would come to this?

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:48.160
It's time to change New Himuka
so our sacrifices won't be in vain.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.830
Someone's... coming.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:03.470
Major General Fubuki!

00:22:03.470 --> 00:22:07.350
I'm so glad I finally found you.

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:09.680
I've been looking for you.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:11.230
Are you all right?

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:13.650
Don't worry about me.

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:16.610
All that matters is we're together now.

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:20.440
We have to find somewhere
safe so I can tell you...

00:22:22.200 --> 00:22:25.870
Major General! Major General Fubuki!

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:41.720
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:51.350
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:53.480
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.980
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:22:55.980 --> 00:23:01.230
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:01.230 --> 00:23:03.030
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:03.030 --> 00:23:05.360
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:10.080
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:15.290
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:20.460
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:24.930
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:30.810
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:32.430
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:35.640
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:37.270
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:37.270 --> 00:23:40.230
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:44.570
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:46.240
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:51.700
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:24:08.510 --> 00:24:11.930
Karen's Wish
